   "source": [
    "PS 1: Python code writing conventions like PEP8(Python Enhancement Proposal 8 for the style guide) highlights are not errors, but rather community agreement of ways of structuring python code for ease of collaboration and standardization. IDEs have inbuilt capability to help developers, but code runs without an error even if you disobey these proposals.\n",
    "You can use linter such as black to format your code automatically to follow style guide convention specified in PEP8.\n",
    "\n",
    "However, it is always advisable to stick to community guidelines and apply the best python practices.\n",
    "\n",
    "PS 2: Conventional commits in version control\n",
    "      A convention for writing commit messages in version control.\n",
    "[Conventional commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/en/v1.0.0/)\n",
    "\n"
   ]
  },
